/**
@file
@brief Subsystem flows and data relationships.

@page diagrams Diagrams

These diagrams summarize the current implementation. Error handling and alternate
paths are shown where they affect ownership or the result; they are not exhaustive
call graphs. See @ref image_display_lifecycle and @ref ownership_and_async for
callback and cancellation details.

@section metadata_write Metadata write sequence

Destination selection is performed by FileData change verification in
@ref filedata.cc; metadata_write_perform() performs the selected write.
Warnings about an unwritable image or sidecar depend on the metadata warning
preference. Falling back to private metadata does not guarantee a successful write.

@startuml
start
:Verify queued metadata change;
if (Save in image file or sidecar enabled?) then (yes)
  if (Direct writing allowed for this file?) then (yes)
    if (Image writable?) then (yes)
      :Select image file;
    else (no)
      :Record warning if enabled;
    endif
  else (no)
    if (Sidecar writing allowed?) then (yes)
      :Resolve matching grouped sidecar or new path\nusing normal or extended XMP naming;
      if (Sidecar writable, or absent with writable parent?) then (yes)
        :Select sidecar;
      else (no)
        :Record warning if enabled;
      endif
    endif
  endif
endif
if (Image or sidecar selected?) then (no)
  :Find existing private XMP metadata when Exiv2 is available;\notherwise, or if absent, try legacy metadata;\nsearch preferred and alternate cache locations;
  if (Existing metadata writable?) then (yes)
    :Select existing private metadata;
  else (no)
    :Create private metadata location using cache preferences;\nchoose .meta or .gq.xmp using legacy-format preference;
    if (Destination writable or can be created?) then (yes)
      :Select private metadata;
    else (no)
      :Report destination permission error;
      stop
    endif
  endif
endif
:Perform selected metadata write;
if (Write succeeds?) then (yes)
  :Remove obsolete legacy metadata;
else (no)
  :Report write failure;
endif
stop
@enduml

Private metadata lookup and creation use cache_find_location() and
cache_create_location(). A legacy .meta file cannot represent an XMP color label;
that write fails rather than silently discarding the label.

@section options_overview Options overview

@ref ConfOptions applies globally; @ref LayoutOptions belongs to each LayoutWindow.
Window creation can also affect global options when a configuration is loaded
with its global section enabled.

@startuml
object "ConfOptions (options.h)" as global_options
object "LayoutWindow" as window
object "LayoutOptions (layout.h)" as layout_options
global_options : Shared through the global options pointer
global_options : Saved in the XML global section
layout_options : One per layout window
layout_options : Saved in that window's XML layout section
window *-- layout_options : options
@enduml

@section options_diagrams_main Options - application startup

The normal GUI startup path uses GtkApplication. A second invocation forwards
its command line to the primary instance; GQ_NEW_INSTANCE requests an independent
instance. Cache-maintenance startup has a separate application path.

@startuml
start
:Create GtkApplication and register handlers;\ng_application_run();
if (Existing primary instance and not independent?) then (yes)
  :Forward command line to primary instance;\nprimary processes requested actions;
  stop
else (no)
  :startup_cb() / startup_common();\nconf_options_new() and setup_default_options();
  :Register application actions;
  :load_options():\nload system geeqierc.xml if present;
  :Load user geeqierc.xml from get_rc_dir();\nuser values follow system values;\nrestore configured layout windows;
  if (No layout window restored?) then (yes)
    :layout_new_from_default();\nload valid default.xml, or use built-in layout;
  endif
  :Process command line and present window;\ncontinue application event loop;
endif
stop
@enduml

Configuration paths are resolved by get_rc_dir(); the diagram deliberately does
not prescribe a separate legacy HOME/.geeqie configuration load.

@section options_diagrams_remote Options - new window from command line

@ref command-line-handling.cc implements gq_new_window(). The primary instance
handles a forwarded request in the same way as a locally delivered command line.

@startuml
start
:gq_new_window();
if (Current layout available?) then (yes)
  :layout_new_from_default();
  if (default.xml loads successfully?) then (yes)
    :Use saved configuration;
  else (no)
    :Create built-in layout;
  endif
  :Assign unique window ID;
  :Set path to requesting process's working directory;
else (no)
  :Return without creating a window;
endif
stop
@enduml

@section options_diagrams_menu Options - new window from menu

The three choices are alternatives, not concurrent operations. See
layout_new_from_default(), @ref layout_menu_window_from_current_cb(), and
@ref layout_menu_window_layout_cb().

@startuml
start
switch (Window creation choice)
case (Default)
  :layout_new_from_default();\nuse valid default.xml or built-in layout;\nassign unique ID;
case (From current)
  :Save current window configuration to temporary XML;\nreplace window ID and load configuration;\npreserve current path or collection when applicable;\nremove temporary files;
case (Named layout)
  if (Layout already displayed or invalid ID?) then (yes)
    :Return without loading;
  else (no)
    :Load named XML from window-layouts directory\nwithout loading global options;
  endif
endswitch
stop
@enduml

@section image_load_overview Image load overview

This sequence follows static-image display. Source preparation occurs before the
worker is queued; decoding and main-context notifications are distinct stages.
See @ref image_display_lifecycle for progressive updates, errors, and cancellation.

@startuml
participant "Layout / ImageWindow\n(main context)" as image
participant "ImageLoader\n(main context)" as loader
participant "Decoder worker" as worker
participant "PixbufRenderer / GTK\n(main context)" as renderer
image -> image : Select file and reset previous load
alt Decoded-image cache hit
  image -> image : Reuse cached pixbuf
else Matching read-ahead work
  image -> image : Adopt completed pixels or running loader
else New load
  image -> loader : image_loader_start_deferred()
  loader -> loader : Deferred start: prepare input_buffer\n(preview or file source)
  loader -> worker : Queue decoding / select backend
end
opt Active decoder
  loop Progressive updates when available
    worker -> loader : Schedule size / area notification
    loader -> image : Main-context callbacks
    image -> renderer : Install pixels / mark changed area
  end
  worker -> loader : Schedule done or error
  loader -> image : Completion callback
  image -> image : Cache completed pixels when enabled;\nrelease active loader; start read-ahead
end
image -> renderer : Prepare display and queue rendering
renderer -> renderer : Scale / post-process / create textures
renderer -> image : Render-complete notification
renderer -> renderer : GTK snapshot and later presentation
note over image, renderer
Progressive rendering overlaps decoding.
Decoder completion and render completion do not measure
compositor presentation. Delayed flipping may retain the old image.
end note
@enduml

@section duplicates_data_layout Duplicates data layout

DupeWindow maintains input lists and comparison results. Each DupeItem owns a
FileData reference and has a list of DupeMatch records pointing to matching items.
These match pointers describe relationships; they do not form an ownership tree.
The second input set is omitted below. group_rank is the average match rank.

@startuml
object DupeWindow
object DupeItem
object DupeMatch
object "Matching DupeItem" as matching
DupeWindow : list = first input set
DupeWindow : second_list = second input set
DupeWindow : dupes = grouped results
DupeItem : fd
DupeItem : group = list of DupeMatch records
DupeItem : group_rank
DupeMatch : di
DupeMatch : rank
DupeWindow --> DupeItem : input / result lists
DupeItem --> DupeMatch : group
DupeMatch --> matching : di (match reference)
@enduml
*/
